<<~ ahu slot=`#/pono-testability-refined-report`>>

! Pono testability: refined report (cold read of Kilo-Scout waves 1+2)

Quill-Reader: Lares (Tasked Spirit), 2026-10-31. Repo read-only; no suites, no Stryker, no edits. Stands alone; the scout's files are untouched.
Persona: Ink-Clerk (grounds, cites, marks testimony) with Council for the ranking.
Ruling folded: operator, 2026-10-31, verbatim "Approve lifting the test re-cut ordering to before founding". The 2026-10-29 "re-cut after the founding" ruling (road lines 268, 849) no longer binds; the road edit rides the next record batch. Every BEFORE tag in the scout's report loses its "needs the lift" clause.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tl-dr`>>

!! TL;DR

# Ratio: tests outnumber code ''1.39-1.41 : 1'' non-comment, ''1.08-1.10 : 1'' raw. Not 1.66. I reproduced the test side to the line (204,872 vs the scout's 204,871; 1,819 test files). Nearest 1.66-ish figure anyone gets: comment-stripped source against raw tests (1.81).
# The Stryker verdict "activates no mutants" has a ''primary-source cause and a shipped fix'': PR #6214 (merged 2026-10-23), in v10.1.0, re-released as 10.1.1. Corrected: the scout cited issue #6262 as the fix's anchor, but #6262 closed as a duplicate of #6210; #6214 is the fix. Source-verified, ''not run-verified'' against vitest 5.0.3: a probe decides.
# The scout missed the sharpest collision: the road gives ''one named owner per step the one compose hunk in `open-node-vessel.ts`'' (road line 312), and that file took ''185 commits since 2026-10-01''. A stage-cut of `prepareNodeBootOn` fights every slice. The road plans no stage-cut (grep: zero hits); the scout's "N/W/H trains already reshape boot" has no support in the road.
# Minimum first lane that earns the early start, touching no hot file: (a) Stryker 10.1.1 probe in a throwaway worktree, (b) one shared scratch fixture piloted on node tests, (c) `LandedLedger.whenLanded`, (d) the real dead-export set (53, not 69). Then characterization tests of the boot sequence, then the stage-cut as a single-owner step.
# Cut from the scout: the fake-timer ban reads as house practice, but 23 files already use fake timers; the `isolate: false` blocker is smaller than stated (8 `stubEnv/stubGlobal` hits in 3 files; the 74 module registries remain the real blocker).

<<~/ahu>>

