<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-the-scout-missed-or-overstated`>>

!! What the scout missed or overstated

# ''Hot-file collision.'' Road line 312 ("the owner law": one named owner per step commits the one compose hunk in `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts`) plus lines 398 and 352 make that file the road's shared bottleneck; 185 commits in 31 days. Any lane that edits it competes with the road; the scout tagged the stage-cut FOLDED without finding this.
# ''No planned stage-cut exists in the road.'' "Fold into the N/W/H trains" is unsupported. The stage-cut would be new road work, an operator decision.
# ''Fake timers.'' 23 files already use `useFakeTimers`/fake-timers (`git grep -l`). The no-global-now law governs product code and decisions ("a wall clock never decides"); a blanket ban on fake timers in tests reads as a new rule. Lean: keep fake timers for third-party timers; for house waits add the event. Do not write "forbidden" into a lane brief.
# ''Dead exports'' shrink 69 to 53, and the barrel-re-exported ones are public API (see above).
# ''Rec 8 (incremental mutation in CI)'' sits well past the pilot; the incremental file is `reports/...` and untracked-by-design; CI cost unknown. Park until the probe numbers exist.
# ''Rec 10 (`isolate: false`)'' blocker stated as "74 registries + stub uses": the stubs are 8 hits in 3 files; registries are the real work. Also `tests/vitest.config.ts:23-29` states `isolate: true` on purpose.
# ''Rec 2 store-ack on the unlock door'' probably lands in or beside the compose hunk (the unlock door sits behind `custody-frames.ts` and the vessel opener). The scout gave it "cost S, BEFORE" without checking which file it touches. Treat as owner-coordinated.
# The scout's ranking put the characterization tests fifth; with the lift, they are the gate for the one L item and belong in the first wave.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ranked-recommendations-as-lanes`>>

!! Ranked recommendations as lanes (re-cut starts now, runs beside the road)

Size: S under a day of lane time, M days, L a train. "Red-first shape" follows `working-procedures.mem`: vector before cure in its own commit, a nonsense control beside each red, assert the setup took. Battery: `mixed-model-swarm.mem #/the-battery` holds (touched packages whole, `lararium-mesh` always, ONE e2e, one heavy battery at a time via `tools/battery.sh`, scratch `HOME`/`LAR_ROOT`, `LAR_BAGS` unset). Large batches per the road until the road edit lands.

!!! Wave A: the minimum first lanes (parallel, none touches `open-node-vessel.ts`)

''A1. Stryker 10.1.1 probe.'' Size S. Throwaway worktree under `~/.lares-scratch/<lane>/wt`; `df` first (WSL VHD law); sandbox mode (default), never `inPlace: true`; local reporters only (never `dashboard`); smallest package first (`memetic-frame` or `mempalace`); sandbox must carry `dist/` (vitest-dist-guard). Question set: does a mutant under `describe` get killed on vitest 5.0.3; does the runner's pool handling survive the repo's config (threads vs forks); per-test kill data present; wall time; disk. Red-first shape: plant ONE known-killable mutant (a flipped comparison in a function with a test) as the red vector and ONE mutant in an uncovered line as the nonsense control; the probe passes only if the first reads Killed and the second reads NoCoverage (watch #6256: a Survived-with-0-tests control means the tool still lies). Files: none tracked (config lives in the throwaway). House law: web3-only (no dashboard), no live-tree mutation. Needs the operator's go for any mutation run (my fence forbade it, not the house); lean yes. Tag: BEFORE, now.

''A2. Shared scratch fixture.'' Size M. `test.extend` fixture with `onCleanup` that makes the temp dir, sets scratch `HOME`, `LAR_ROOT`, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` and restores them. Pilot on ~20 node test files, measure the LOC drop, then codemod by package (1,057 `mkdtemp` sites). Files: `packages/lararium-node/tests/support/scratch-custody-setup.ts` (108 lines, the one existing seed), `tests/harness/with-lar-root.ts` (its header names the env-mutation and "NOT thread-safe" hazard), the pilot test files. Red-first shape: a test that leaks (sets `LAR_ROOT` and forgets restore, or reads the real `homedir`) is the red; the control is a fixture-using twin that stays green; assert the setup took by reading the env inside the test. Touches no product file. Tag: BEFORE, now.

''A3. `LandedLedger.whenLanded` and the poll sweep it enables.'' Size S. Files: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/landed-ledger.ts` (14 lines), `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/wiki-shore-draft-road.test.ts` (:463, :466, :633 poll loops) and the other `wiki-shore-*` tests. Red-first shape: a vector where the landing arrives late (deferred past the old 2 s poll) reds the poll form; the cure is the event; the control is a title that never lands, which must time out with a named refusal, not hang. Clock stays injected; no `useFakeTimers` needed. Tag: BEFORE, now. Collision: none with the stage-cut.

''A4. Dead-export sweep, one batch.'' Size S. Delete the 53 nowhere-referenced exports (list in this report's section above; regenerate from a fresh tree before the lane starts since 185 commits a month move it). Keep barrel re-exports unless the operator rules the barrel surface. Red-first shape: the existing typecheck witness plus `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` is the control; the red is a compile of the tree with the delete applied to a name that still has a consumer (prove the instrument bites before trusting its zero). Files: about 45 `src/*.ts` across mesh, node, mempalace, tw5, cli, sensorium (none in `open-node-vessel.ts`). Collision: merge noise with in-flight lanes; land as a single batch right after a controller land, announce it. Tag: BEFORE, now.

!!! Wave B: after A2/A3 land, still beside the road

''B1. Characterization tests of the boot sequence.'' Size M. Test-only: pin the observable order and outputs of `prepareNodeBootOn` / `composeNodeVesselOn` (stages, teardown on refuse, what listeners and store names exist after) and the same for `open-browser-vessel.ts`. Files: new tests under `packages/lararium-node/tests/` and `packages/lararium-browser/tests/`; reads `open-node-vessel.ts`, never edits it. Red-first shape: this IS the red-first control for the later cut: each pin lands with a mutant that breaks the order (run via the A1 probe or the hand-catalog pattern `tools/law-mutants.mjs`) and the pin must go red; the control stays red after the cut (per `working-procedures.mem`). Risk: other slices legitimately change boot behavior and red the pins. Pin stage order and port contracts, not every field, and let the compose-hunk owner update a pin in the same commit. Tag: BEFORE the stage-cut; collision: none with the file, but it couples to every slice that changes boot.

''B2. Eventful seams for the other flake families.'' Size S each. (i) TW5 dropdown: ready attribute from the served page after the worker settles plus failure artifacts (`browserConsole`, mirror DOM) in `packages/lararium-web/tests/e2e/shore-writes.e2e.test.ts:150-164`. (ii) Browser two-tab unlock: event in `browser-tab-custody` test. (iii) Staged-unlock store-ack: the door and `tests/harness/instance.ts`. ''(iii) probably touches the compose hunk or `custody-frames.ts`: route it through the compose-hunk owner.'' Red-first shape per item: a late-event vector reds the fixed-wait form, a never-event control must fail loudly and name the missing edge. Tag: BEFORE, now (i, ii); (iii) coordinate.

''B3. Test-only export list and `testing` subpath.'' Size S (list), M (moves). Compiler-based list (the scout's regex list stays candidates). Moves ride module cuts, so they cannot ride the stage-cut lane; do per package after the owner window. Tag: list now, moves FOLDED into whichever lane cuts that module.

!!! Wave C: the L item and what waits

''C1. Stage-cut `prepareNodeBootOn`'' (and `open-browser-vessel.ts`) into typed stages with a `Ports` record. Size L. Land whole, never half-injected ("Full models land early", and "Old shapes burn": no second shape, no shim). ''Collides with the road's owner law and 185 recent commits.'' It cannot run beside slices that edit the compose hunk; it needs the compose-hunk owner seat for a window, or it belongs to the first quiet step between slices. Lean: schedule as one named road step after B1, owner = this lane, every other lane stops at module boundaries for its duration. Whether it runs before the founding is the operator's call; it stays out of Wave A/B either way. Files: `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`, `packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`, B1's pins.

''C2. Inject homes and the operator hint'' (identity/storage/seal dirs, `readLocalOperatorHint`), retiring `withLarRoot` env mutation and the git-global shell-out. Size M. Needs A2 first. ''Touches the opener's options and `node-host.ts`/`vessel-paths.ts`: sequence with C1'' (same file family) or fold into it. Files: `open-node-vessel.ts`, `vessel-paths.ts`, `node-host.ts`, `tests/harness/with-lar-root.ts`. Red-first shape: a test that opens a vessel with injected homes and asserts the real home stays untouched (the leak is the red; a control with the env path stays green until retired).

''C3. Mutation as an inspection list.'' Size M. After A1 reads green. Per package `mutate` ranges, `perTest`, local `html`/`json` reporters; read surviving mutants, list zero-kill tests as a review list, whitelist controls and seeds, never auto-delete. Watch #6256 (NoCoverage reported as Survived). Tag: AFTER the probe, may run beside the road; no CI wiring until A1 reports cost.

''C4. Extend the law pattern'' (fast-check + seeds + control + named mutants) to `tw5` wiki-shore vectors and `mesh` face-gate / content-key-holder (test files of 1,000-1,300 lines). Size M per package. One pilot may start as soon as A1 lands, so a real runner scores it; fixed seed stays.

''C5. Unit shards and `isolate: false`.'' Size M. Blocked by the 74 module-level Maps/Sets (the stub APIs are minor). Extend `tools/e2e-shards.mjs` for timed unit shards. After C1/C2 (registries move to the composition root).

''C6. Witness consolidation.'' Size S-M. Low value; park.

''C7. Report the ratio as non-comment; add runtime per claim, co-change churn, flake sightings per test.'' Size 0. Now.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/operator-asks-each-with-a-lean`>>

!! Operator asks, each with a lean

# ''Reorg before the founding?'' Yes for the seam-opening work (Waves A and B) and the characterization tests: they touch no hot file, change no product shape, and earn the early start. The stage-cut (C1) is the real question: lean yes only as a single-owner road step with a freeze on the compose hunk; no, if the road would stall for it. Minimum set that earns the early start: A1 + A2 + A3 + B1.
# ''Lift the road ruling?'' Done (2026-10-31). Left to edit: road lines 268 and 849 (record batch). Nothing else in the scout's plan needs a lift.
# ''Go for a mutation run?'' The house law allows it in a sandbox in a throwaway worktree; my fence did not. Lean: approve A1 as scoped (one small package, sandbox, local reporters, `df` first).
# ''Stage-cut in the road?'' The road names none. Needs a ruling: does the compose-hunk owner law (road :312) give the cut a window, and who owns it? Lean: a named step after B1.
# ''Delete the barrel-re-exported unused exports?'' Barrel names are public surface. Lean: delete the 53 nowhere names now; rule the 16 barrel/other-used ones separately (they may be intended API for the second operator).
# ''Fake timers.'' Lean: no new ban; the rule is "a house wait gets an event; fake timers only for timers the house does not own".
# ''The 1.66 figure.'' Not reproduced; give the operator 1.39-1.41 non-comment as the number, and note the ratio has no outside norm. Do not make 1.66 a target.

<<~/ahu>>

