!! Testimony (not verified)

* Where 1.66 came from; the prior scout's 233 method; the Stryker version that produced canon's "no mutants" verdict (very likely 10.0.0).
* The ~350 strict test-only exports and ~1,198 loose; the 54-witness and overlap claims; `contract-witness.sh` vs `nexus-two-root` overlap.
* Whether 10.1.1 runs clean on this repo's vitest 5.0.3, and whether it handles the heavy suites' pool.
* DocHandle event semantics at automerge-repo 2.6.0-alpha.5.
* Cost sizes S/M/L in this report: my estimates from file counts and touched surfaces, no timing data.
* The compose-hunk collision severity: 185 commits is a count of commits touching the file, not of conflicts; the lane owner can measure real conflict rate before choosing C1's window.

